<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-8421] ZkDistributedCollectDataFuture fails to delete future data in case of concurrent deletion</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-8421</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;In &lt;b&gt;ZkDistributedCollectDataFuture#deleteFutureData&lt;/b&gt; method KeeperException.NoNodeException may be thrown but the exception isn&apos;t critical in this context and doesn&apos;t require special handling (just logging is enough).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However &lt;b&gt;deleteFutureData&lt;/b&gt; relies on &lt;b&gt;ZookeeperClient#getChildren&lt;/b&gt; which reacts on any exception (including NoNodeException) by killing current Ignite node.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Another implementation of &lt;b&gt;ZookeeperClient#getChildren&lt;/b&gt; is needed which tolerates NoNodeException.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="13155908">IGNITE-8421</key>
            <summary>ZkDistributedCollectDataFuture fails to delete future data in case of concurrent deletion</summary>
